    <string name="menus_about_title">Phosphor · independent implementation</string>
    <string name="menus_about_body">Native terminal launcher inspired by phosphor.zanoski.com. Not the original commercial app or affiliated with its author.\n\nNo ads, accounts or analytics. Apps, calendar, notes and notifications remain on this device. Weather sends the chosen city to Open-Meteo geocoding and coordinates to Open-Meteo forecasts. If that forecast service is unreachable, coordinates are sent to wttr.in instead. Device location is rounded to two decimals; weather is requested only when configured.\n\nascii.rest artwork by @bas3line is bundled under the MIT license and plays entirely offline. License: settings → ASCII art.\n\nSwipe ↑ apps · ↓ system shade · ← → pages. Hold blank space for pages; hold an app for dock/favorites/info/uninstall. All permissions are optional.</string>
